d{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRotating the vector ${r}^{′}(t)$ by ${90}^{∘}$ clockwise, we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Finally, we normalize the vector found in step 2.\n\nNote that the magnitude of the vector found in step 2 equals the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(t)$ (since they differ only by a rotation). Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =\\frac{1}{||{r}^{′}(t)||}[\\begin{aligned}6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j}{||{r}^{′}(t)||}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that $b(t)=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.$" 13194139535807 true] [17592186367396 1000 #edb/ref 17592186367397 13194139535807 true] [17592186367396 1000 #edb/ref 17592186367398 13194139535807 true] [17592186367396 1000 #edb/ref 17592186367399 13194139535807 true] [17592186367396 1000 #edb/ref 17592186367400 13194139535807 true] [17592186367396 1000 #edb/ref 17592186367401 13194139535807 true] [17592186367396 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535807 true] [17592186367396 1041 "selection" 13194139535807 true] [17592186367396 1104 #edb/ref 17592186367398 13194139535807 true] [17592186367396 1110 #uuid "4a9a599e-0887-532e-b219-a52806bdc8ce" 13194139535807 true] [17592186367397 1034 "6\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" 13194139535807 true] [17592186367397 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535807 true] [17592186367397 1111 #uuid "b66d3403-d1ff-5652-97ef-b5fc07e9083a" 13194139535807 true] [17592186367398 1034 "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" 13194139535807 true] [17592186367398 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535807 true] [17592186367398 1111 #uuid "9b02fc59-0ee5-5f88-aa22-a383ea9ef6a7" 13194139535807 true] [17592186367399 1034 "-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t" 13194139535807 true] [17592186367399 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 131941